        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(state): run additive column migration before canonical schema assertion",
        "body": "Closes #109867\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nAfter upgrading from `2026.7.2-beta.1` to `2026.7.2-beta.2`, `openclaw doctor --fix` fails with `Error: no such column: agent_id` and the gateway cannot start.\n\n**Root cause:** In `repairOpenClawStateDatabaseSchema()`, `assertCanonicalStateSchemaShape()` was called BEFORE `ensureAdditiveStateColumns()`. The canonical schema DDL creates indexes on `managed_outgoing_image_records.agent_id`, but that column is added later by `ensureAdditiveStateColumns()`. Result: `no such column: agent_id`.\n\n**Note:** The sister function `ensureSchema()` (used for fresh/upgraded databases at line 243) already has the correct order — `ensureAdditiveStateColumns()` before `assertCanonicalStateSchemaShape()`. This PR makes the `repairOpenClawStateDatabaseSchema()` path consistent.\n\n**Fix (1 file, -1/+1 line):** Swap the two lines in `repairOpenClawStateDatabaseSchema()` so `ensureAdditiveStateColumns(db)` runs before `assertCanonicalStateSchemaShape(db, pathname)`, matching the already-correct order in `ensureSchema()`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Code-level: Before/After ordering\n\n**BEFORE (BUG)** — `repairOpenClawStateDatabaseSchema()` at src/state/openclaw-state-db.ts:\n```typescript\nassertCanonicalStateSchemaShape(db, pathname);  // ❌ creates indexes on agent_id\nif (tableExists(db, \"audit_events\")) {\n  ensureAdditiveStateColumns(db);               // ❌ adds agent_id TOO LATE\n  db.exec(OPENCLAW_STATE_SCHEMA_SQL);\n  ...\n}\n```\n\n**AFTER (FIXED)** — matches `ensureSchema()` order:\n```typescript\nensureAdditiveStateColumns(db);                  // ✅ add columns FIRST\nassertCanonicalStateSchemaShape(db, pathname);   // ✅ now indexes can reference agent_id\nif (tableExists(db, \"audit_events\")) {\n  db.exec(OPENCLAW_STATE_SCHEMA_SQL);\n  ...\n}\n```\n\n### Cross-reference: ensureSchema() already correct\n\nThe `ensureSchema()` function (line 243-245, used for fresh database opens) already has the correct order and has been working without issue:\n```typescript\n// ensureSchema — already correct since beta.2 shipped\nensureAdditiveStateColumns(db);                  // line 243\nassertCanonicalStateSchemaShape(db, pathname);  // line 245\n```\n\nThis PR makes `repairOpenClawStateDatabaseSchema()` consistent with the already-working `ensureSchema()` path.\n\n### Issue reporter verification\n\nThe issue reporter manually verified the fix by running the equivalent of `ensureAdditiveStateColumns` before `assertCanonicalStateSchemaShape`:\n\n```sql\nALTER TABLE managed_outgoing_image_records ADD COLUMN original_media_root TEXT NOT NULL;\nALTER TABLE managed_outgoing_image_records ADD COLUMN agent_id TEXT;\nALTER TABLE managed_outgoing_image_records ADD COLUMN cleanup_pending INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 CHECK (cleanup_pending IN (0, 1));\n```\n\nThen `openclaw doctor --fix --non-interactive` completed successfully and `openclaw gateway status --deep` reported `Runtime: running`.\n\n### Diff\n\n```\nsrc/state/openclaw-state-db.ts | 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)\n```\n\n- oxfmt: clean\n- Change is exactly: move `ensureAdditiveStateColumns(db)` one line up, before `assertCanonicalStateSchemaShape`",
